 "CourseInfo": "Wilson opened in 1927 as part of George C. Thomas Jr.'s 36-hole plan for Griffith Park, and it plays 7,002 yards from the Black tees. Griffith Park hosted the Los Angeles Open from 1937 to 1939. In 1938 Babe Didrikson played in it, the first woman to play in an official PGA Tour event. Eleven of Thomas's original holes remain on this par-72 piece of Los Angeles golf history.",
